id: E703
draft: true
severity: 2
category: conan|meson|ohos|pkg-config|linkage
trigger_tool: conan|meson
phase: configure|build|consumer
keywords: Windows host, OHOS, MesonToolchain, PkgConfigDeps, VirtualRunEnv, conanrun, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, pkg-config, pkgconf, llvm-ar, llvm-ranlib, transitive_libs, proxy-libintl, intl, Conan consumer, sysroot, cross_building, SONAME symlink, loader file identity
error_signature: Meson cross build cannot resolve generated dependency modules|generated .pc files expose bare -lintl|archive tool missing|consumer link fails with unresolved intl or GLib symbols|native OHOS worker rejects test_package with tools.build:sysroot is required|consumer links but target test_package cannot load the tested shared-library SONAME under conanrun|inline LD_LIBRARY_PATH assignment is not exported by the target shell|Windows self.run reports '. is not recognized' before Meson starts|extensionless GLib generator scripts are not executable on a Windows host|CI consumer test returns 127 with missing shared-library SONAME despite a logged LD_LIBRARY_PATH
match_keywords: Windows-hosted OHOS cross build, native OHOS worker, Meson machine files, generated pkg-config modules, archive tools, public transitive dependencies, consumer link closure, conditional sysroot, Conan environment wrapper, extensionless host generator
root_cause: A Windows-hosted OHOS Meson build has two separate boundaries: host-side tools used while configuring and generating code, and target-side libraries exported to consumers. Supplying only a cross compiler or only .pc files leaves Meson without pkg-config/archive tools, while declaring intl as a system name or a bare -lintl loses the task-owned provider path and breaks the consumer closure. Conan may generate only POSIX .sh environment files for an OHOS host profile; the default self.run() wrapper then sends '. ".../conanbuild.sh"' to Windows cmd.exe, failing before the command starts. GLib generator entries can also be extensionless Python scripts, which Windows Meson cannot execute directly. Native OHOS workers may provide a compiler-default sysroot without exposing tools.build:sysroot; requiring that conf unconditionally rejects a valid native profile. Separately, a test_package that calls self.run(..., env="conanrun") without generating VirtualRunEnv receives no package runtime path; even when the direct package exports runenv_info, transitive shared-library libdirs are not guaranteed to be present in the generated shell environment. On some target shells, an inline assignment with shell parameter expansion is logged but is not exported as a loader environment, so the runtime closure must be exported explicitly before exec. A native OHOS worker can also run clang while its lld helper cannot load an SDK-side libxml2; the consumer compile subprocess must prepend the compiler-adjacent SDK lib/lib64 directories to its host-tool LD_LIBRARY_PATH without applying that path to the target consumer runtime.
rec_approach: Bind host tools in generated Meson machine files, fail closed when pkg-config/pkgconf is absent, configure the target prefix as '/', and expose GLib plus the actual intl provider as Conan transitive requirements. On Windows/OHOS, generate task-owned .cmd wrappers only for extensionless host scripts and run Meson commands with env=None so Conan does not apply a POSIX .sh wrapper to cmd.exe; retain the normal environment wrapper on POSIX workers. Require tools.build:sysroot only when cross_building(self) is true; otherwise let the native OHOS compiler use its default sysroot. If a sysroot is present, pass it explicitly. Ensure generated pkg-config data carries provider library directories and static-compilation defines. For runnable shared-library consumers, generate VirtualRunEnv, derive an absolute de-duplicated runtime closure from the tested package and non-build/non-test Conan dependency libdirs, stage the shared objects beside the consumer under a task-private runtime directory, bind one DT_RPATH containing both $ORIGIN/runtime and the absolute staging path, verify each staged entry is a non-empty readable regular file, and still use an explicit `export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=... && executable` command before execution. The origin-relative entry is required because a worker may execute the consumer in a loader namespace where its absolute Conan cache path is not visible; the ordinary directory name avoids a loader boundary observed with the hidden directory.
rec_description: |
  For Windows-hosted OHOS recipes that use MesonToolchain and PkgConfigDeps, inject
  pkg-config/pkgconf plus llvm-ar/llvm-ranlib into the generated machine files and
  keep host tool paths separate from target sysroot paths. Do not use a system_libs
  projection for a Conan-provided intl implementation. The package_info component
  must expose the real provider with transitive headers/libs, and the test_package
  must query the generated pkg-config module and compile a source file that calls
  the package API.
rec_command: |
  # after PkgConfigDeps(self).generate():
  #   validate pkg-config/pkgconf, inject pkg-config, ar and ranlib into both
  #   Meson native/cross machine files, and use --prefix=/ for OHOS setup.
  # in requirements/package_info:
  #   self.requires("glib/...", transitive_headers=True, transitive_libs=True)
  #   self.requires("proxy-libintl/...", transitive_headers=True, transitive_libs=True)
  #   expose the provider component instead of system_libs=["intl"]
  # in test_package:
  #   generate VirtualRunEnv, derive tested-package-first absolute libdirs from
  #   non-build/non-test dependencies, copy the shared-library closure beside
  #   the consumer under .runtime, bind one DT_RPATH to that directory, and
  #   run with conanrun plus an explicit exported LD_LIBRARY_PATH assignment;
  #   run pkg-config --cflags --libs json-glib-1.0 and compile a real API consumer;
  #   require tools.build:sysroot only for cross_building(self), and append it
  #   only when configured so native OHOS workers use the compiler default.
rec_auto_fix: false
affected_scope: Windows-hosted Conan recipes for OHOS libraries built by Meson when generated pkg-config modules and target-provided transitive libraries are consumed by a real downstream program.
verification_cmd: meson test -C <build> --print-errorlogs --num-processes 2 && conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<host-profile> --build=missing
verification_evidence: json-glib/1.10.8 local-r014 RC 0 after adding VirtualRunEnv and tested-first runtime libdir closure; local-r016 reproduced the Windows '. is not recognized' environment-wrapper failure; local-r017 rebuilt the current recipe revision with task-owned host wrappers, returned RC 0, ran the 55-step Meson build, materialized both SONAME aliases, and passed consumer compile/link; package readback shows three regular 188808-byte files with identical SHA-256; runtime-path fixture PASS with build/test dependency exclusion and de-duplication; CI #49167 showed the target shell did not honor the inline parameter expansion, so the follow-up uses explicit export; upstream 17/17; CI #50036 build 57257 reached conan-build-test and failed only while running test_package because libjson-glib-1.0.so.0 was not found and the json_* symbols remained unresolved (RC 127), proving link success without a loader-bound runtime closure; current-head CI #50093 build 57314 confirmed the single DT_RPATH and DT_NEEDED readback but still failed to load the cache-path SONAME, proving that the worker runtime boundary also requires a task-private staged shared-library directory; CI #50100 build 57321 then showed a native OHOS worker whose lld could not load SDK-side libxml2 during consumer linking, so host-tool runtime paths are a separate contract from target RPATH; CI #50108 build 57329 reproduced the same failure after absolute staging, and CI #50137 build 57368 reproduced it again with $ORIGIN/.runtime plus absolute staging, despite correct DT_RPATH and explicit LD_LIBRARY_PATH; the successor changes the task-private directory to ordinary runtime, validates each staged file as non-empty/readable/regular, keeps the staged non-build/non-test closure first in LD_LIBRARY_PATH, checks DT_NEEDED for libjson-glib-1.0.so.0, and prepends compiler-adjacent SDK lib/lib64 directories only for clang/readelf subprocesses; local AArch64 OHOS hand-link readback confirmed DT_RPATH, no DT_RUNPATH, and DT_NEEDED for libjson-glib-1.0.so.0, while local Windows-hosted OHOS conan create local-win-r021 returned RC 0; a new W3 successor and current-head platform CI are required.
authors:
  - 2301_80739235
execution_boundary_root_cause: Conan workers can recreate the test build folder between build() and test(), so a runtime directory validated only during build can be absent when the consumer executes.
execution_boundary_fix: Re-run the same filtered idempotent staging helper immediately before consumer execution, require a non-empty result, and prepend that directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH without importing host SDK libraries.
execution_boundary_evidence: Windows-hosted OHOS conan create returned RC 0; USB HDC W3 r035 used one launch and passed Harmony programs 3/3, state checks 7/7, consumer 1/1, assertions 8/8, complete 12-receipt validation, post-release validation, and retirement for candidate tree 3a0851d2c21f152e2d1455d9379e66faab56ce1a; r034 is retained as a terminal pre-transfer host-runtime failure with launch_count=0 and cleanup PASS.
loader_identity_root_cause: Native OHOS CI can reject a byte-identical regular-file copy even when the staged inventory, DT_RPATH and exported LD_LIBRARY_PATH are correct; CI 60571 disproved symlink preservation alone, narrowing the remaining boundary to the installed versioned ELF identity lost when the package file is copied.
loader_identity_fix: Native POSIX OHOS package() no longer forces a build/package ELF hardlink. It retains the complete Meson-installed SONAME alias chain only after samefile and byte/mode validation; test_package runtime staging uses verified byte copies so cross-filesystem and worker hardlink capability differences do not block packaging. Keep regular-file materialization for Windows-hosted cross builds where target execution does not occur.
loader_identity_evidence: CI 60550/Buildbot 69281 and CI 60571/Buildbot 69302 on prior/current heads logged correct staging, RPATH and export yet failed to load libjson-glib-1.0.so.0; CI 61372/worker OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper-CI-028 returned Operation not permitted while forcing an alias hardlink; CI 61434 on HEAD 525711869e65612133a6f6fc4ea4b86a2aad04b0 rejected the native build/package hardlink because st_dev differed after 17/17 upstream tests passed. The merged recipe removes native hardlink rebinding, keeps verified SONAME symlinks, and local Windows OHOS `local-win-r045-no-native-hardlink` returned RC 0 with recipe RREV b2ccb948a96ca4edd87b5837b28b3522 and package revision a90dee4bf4f018466b9a28b5932d32f2. A new USB HDC W3 successor, current-head platform CI and AI Review remain required.
